==================================================================================================
0. HOW TO READ THIS FILE
==================================================================================================

NOTATION   This file reuses the local declarative notation of Artifact 067, with the CHECK line
           Artifact 069 added, the REPOSITORY CONVENTION basis label Artifact 071 added, and the
           absent word Artifact 073 added. It is an implementation choice, not COOLBOY12
           architecture, and establishes no repository-wide schema language (SC-077-J). No
           parser exists for it.

           ELEMENT <name>        a structural element of a materialized Record
           ELEMENT <a>.<b>       part <b> of each value of element <a>: structure inside that
                                 one family element, not a separate family element
           LAYER                 ENVELOPE (universal, RMS §4) or FAMILY (Registry-model-owned)
           REQUIRED              yes | no — no element of this family is conditional
           CARDINALITY           exactly-one | zero-or-one | zero-or-more | one-or-more — the
                                 count of the carrier in the Record, never the count of Models,
                                 Kinds or fields the defined schema may name (§1)
           CONSTRAINT            what a conforming value must satisfy
           CHECK                 how the constraint is checked, as Artifact 069 defines it:
                                   NATIVE    decidable from the Record alone
                                   EXTERNAL  needs evidence outside the Record; the line names
                                             who supplies it, and this contract does not claim
                                             it proven
                                   STATIC    a property of this contract, checked by reading it
           BASIS                 where the element or rule comes from:
                                   SOURCE FACT            stated by a governing source
                                   REQUIRED SYNTHESIS     forced by several source facts together
                                   REPOSITORY CONVENTION  a choice of Artifact 067, 069, 071 or
                                                          073, reused
                                   077 CHOICE             a representation decision of this file
           REJECT                a value that does not conform, with the rule it breaks and its
                                 CHECK

           Dotted parts, zero-or-one, zero-or-more and one-or-more are this file's additions to
           the notation, a 077 choice: SCHEMA-DEFINITION is the first family whose content is a
           list of like entries — applicability targets and field occurrences (§3).

OUTCOMES   A candidate Record has exactly one of four outcomes under this contract. They are
           decided in this order, and the first that applies is the outcome (§4 A-10):
             REJECT            a rule is shown to be violated: a NATIVE rule fails; an EXTERNAL
                               check establishes a violation; or a status that must be
                               established — the declared status of a named Kind, or the
                               admissible category of a reference actually carried — cannot
                               be established when its owner's check is run: "Undetermined is
                               not permitted." (Artifact 063 RB-6). An open shape never hides
                               a violation.
             UNRESOLVED        no violation is shown, but the Record has a shape whose
                               admissibility the governing sources leave open: a Model-level
                               or several-target applicability (§4 A-08, A-09; 076 SC-076-N;
                               SC-077-C), or no field occurrence (§4 O-01; SC-077-O). This
                               contract neither accepts nor rejects the shape, and a carrier
                               able to hold it is no authority for it. It is not a success;
                               EXTERNAL evidence still pending is recorded beside it.
             PENDING_EXTERNAL  every NATIVE rule holds and no shape is UNRESOLVED, but one or
                               more EXTERNAL checks have not yet been established. A pre-final
                               evidence state, not acceptance: it becomes CONFORMS only when
                               the owners' evidence establishes every check, and REJECT when
                               that evidence shows a violation or, under RB-6, cannot
                               establish a required status.
             CONFORMS          every NATIVE rule holds, every applicable EXTERNAL check has
                               been established by its owner, no shape is UNRESOLVED, and no
                               rule is violated.
           Three evidence states stay apart. Not yet checked: PENDING_EXTERNAL. Checked, but a
           required status cannot be established: REJECT for a named Kind or a carried reference
           (RB-6); for any other EXTERNAL obligation the Record is not accepted — it stays
           PENDING_EXTERNAL, never CONFORMS. Checked and shown invalid: REJECT. A NATIVE pass
           alone is never CONFORMS.
           The four labels, their order and the PENDING_EXTERNAL state are 077 CHOICES; RB-6 is
           Artifact 063's. They exist so that structural representability is never read as
           semantic legality, in either direction. This file states the decision; it implements
           no validator (§6 EXECUTION), and no outcome named here reports a real Record.

STATUS     This contract describes the structure a materialized SCHEMA-DEFINITION Record must
           satisfy. It is not a SCHEMA-DEFINITION Record, not the schema of any Record of W, E,
           P, V or I, not a model-owned schema such as row 184's CHARACTER schema, not a
           validator, a schema engine or a Registry service, and not canonical data. It is an
           authored source outside canon/** (Roadmap §0.8; CONFLICT-F), and not a
           canonicalization source. Concrete SCHEMA-DEFINITION Records are committed only
           through the Mutation Coordinator (row 152) after G-CANON-R. Where this contract
           differs from the Master Blueprint, the Record Model System, the Roadmap, or Artifact
           076, those sources are right and this contract is wrong.

SPEC       Artifact 076 — docs/registry/schema_definition.md — is the semantic contract this file
           encodes, consumed unchanged (H: 076). This file encodes only the structural
           consequences of the obligations 076 establishes and hands to 077 (076 §21). Artifacts
           067, 069, 071 and 073 are precedents for notation and representation conventions
           only: no semantics is taken from the MODEL-, KIND-, SUBTYPE- or FIELD-DEFINITION
           families, and none of those rows is a dependency of row 077.

==================================================================================================
1. RECORD SHAPE
==================================================================================================

SCHEMA-DEFINITION RECORD
├── ENVELOPE  partition · kind · object_id · slug · provenance · registry_ref · sot_class
└── FAMILY    applicability · occurrence · definition
              ├── applicability   one or more targets, each:   model · kind (zero or one)
              ├── occurrence      zero or more entries, each:  field · required · cardinality
              └── definition      the governed account of the schema as one definition

Artifact 077 defines exactly these ten elements: the universal seven-field envelope (RMS §4) and
three family elements. The family elements have five parts in all — two of applicability and
three of occurrence; definition has none. It defines no other element or part.

That is the scope boundary of this contract, not a closure over everything a SCHEMA-DEFINITION
Record may later carry. Rows 108–110 keep their authority to establish Registry-owned evolution,
versioning, supersession and deprecation representation (§6 VERSIONABILITY; 076 VS-076-2). The
envelope, by contrast, stays exactly seven fields: no downstream Registry representation becomes
an eighth universal field (RMS §4; P-05).

One schema, three carriers. 076 requires that a SCHEMA-DEFINITION govern the definition of one
schema — "the structure the schema defines and the scope to which that structure applies" (076
§6). This contract carries the scope in applicability, the field composition in occurrence, and
the governed account of the schema in definition. No carrier alone is the schema definition.

Carrier count is not semantic count. applicability can hold more than one target, and a target
can omit kind. That makes two shapes representable — several scopes, and a scope at Model level
without a Kind. It does not make either admissible: how many Models and Kinds a schema may name,
and whether both categories are always present, is not established (076 SC-076-N). §4 marks both
shapes UNRESOLVED. The one applicability shape this contract treats as admissible is the shape
076 shows as legal: one target naming a declared Kind of its declared model (076 §17 A); a Record
of that shape still reaches CONFORMS only once its EXTERNAL checks are established (§0).
occurrence can likewise be empty. A Record listing no field occurrence is representable and
UNRESOLVED — not accepted and not rejected (§4 O-01; SC-077-O).

Two roles of "kind", never merged. The envelope element kind names this Record's own Kind —
always SCHEMA-DEFINITION. applicability.kind names a declared Kind the schema applies to — for
example CHARACTER. They are different elements in different roles, and neither is a
two-character kind code.

Not the Records it applies to. A Character Record conforms, or fails to conform, to a schema; it
stays World's either way (076 §13). This contract is the structure of the Registry Record that
defines the schema, not of any Record the schema applies to, and it defines no field of any
model's Records (P-04).

==================================================================================================
2. ENVELOPE — the universal seven (RMS §4; Artifact 033)
==================================================================================================

Types, defaults, nullability and serialization of the envelope fields are not established by the
governing sources (Artifact 033) and are not stated here.

ELEMENT     partition
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  R — the Registry partition
CHECK       NATIVE
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — "SCHEMA-DEFINITION is a Registry Record." (RMS §10.2); RMS §10.1; 076
            §6, SD-1
REJECT      W, E, P, V or I — a Record of a domain model, such as a World Character Record, is
            never a SCHEMA-DEFINITION                             (SD-1, SD-9)      NATIVE

ELEMENT     kind
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  identifies the declared Registry Kind SCHEMA-DEFINITION (Kind 5 of RMS §10.1) — this
            Record's own Kind, never the Kind the schema applies to (076 §14). The constraint is
            symbolic. No two-character Registry Kind code is established; none is minted here
            (SC-077-I).
CHECK       NATIVE against the symbolic Kind; against a code only once the Registry's codes are
            bound by their own rows (row 117; Artifact 060 writes the code schematically as <kind>)
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §10.1; Artifact 064 §12; 076 §14, SD-11
REJECT      FIELD-DEFINITION — field meaning is another Registry Kind (SD-3)       NATIVE
            CONSTRAINT-DEFINITION or VALIDATION-RULE — a condition or a check is another
            Registry Kind                                         (SD-6)            NATIVE
            CONTROLLED-VOCABULARY, KIND-DEFINITION or any other Registry Kind      NATIVE
            a domain Kind (for example CHARACTER) placed here     (076 §14)         NATIVE
            any invented code (for example SD) presented as established            NATIVE

ELEMENT     object_id
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  the object identity component under the universal identity grammar. It is this
            Record's identity — not the schema's name or label, not a field name, not the
            identity of an applicable Kind or of any Record of it, not a file name, and not the
            identity of any implementation that checks the schema (076 RS-076-2, SD-2).
CHECK       NATIVE — presence, a single value
            STATIC — this contract makes no family element a substitute for it
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §4, §5; 076 RS-076-1, RS-076-2

ELEMENT     slug
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  decoration only; never identity, never the basis of resolution
CHECK       NATIVE — presence, a single value
            STATIC — this contract gives slug no identity or resolution role
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §5; Artifact 033; 076 RS-076-2

ELEMENT     provenance
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  as the universal envelope carries it: this Record's own provenance capture.
            Provenance meaning is not defined here, and the provenance of a Record the schema
            applies to is never carried here.
CHECK       NATIVE for presence
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §4; Artifact 033

ELEMENT     registry_ref
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  the universal envelope field, unchanged. This contract attaches no referent,
            self-reference convention, bootstrap target or resolution meaning to it, and it
            carries neither the schema's applicability nor any field it composes.
CHECK       NATIVE for presence
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §4; Artifact 033 leaves its referent unresolved; Blueprint §9.4:
            "Reference resolution is not Registry work"

ELEMENT     sot_class
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  as the universal envelope carries it. No value is fixed here; Artifact 077's own
            manifest SoT and Canon are not Record-level values and are not copied into it.
CHECK       NATIVE for presence
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §4; Artifact 033

==================================================================================================
3. FAMILY — SCHEMA-DEFINITION content (Registry-model-owned; not envelope fields)
==================================================================================================

applicability and definition are required; occurrence may hold no entry, a shape §4 O-01 marks
UNRESOLVED. No family element or part has a default value. A required element or part may not be
left empty, and an absent part is absent — not an empty value, a null placeholder or a wildcard
(REPOSITORY CONVENTION, 073). Types and serialization of the family elements are not established
by the governing sources and are not stated here; this contract fixes structure, not an
encoding.

ELEMENT     applicability
LAYER       FAMILY
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY one-or-more — each value is one applicability target, with the parts
            applicability.model and applicability.kind
CONSTRAINT  each target states one scope the schema applies to, through RMS §10.2's
            "applicable Model · applicable Kind": a declared Record Model and, for a Kind-scoped
            target, a declared Kind of that model.
            At least one. 076 §7: every SCHEMA-DEFINITION "states the structure its schema
            defines and the declared scope it applies to", and SD-4 states that scope through the
            applicable-Model and applicable-Kind categories. A Record with no target states no
            scope.
            No count beyond one is fixed. A second target, or a target without kind, is
            representable and UNRESOLVED (§4 A-08, A-09): this contract does not establish that
            a schema may apply to several scopes or at Model level, and does not establish that
            it may not (076 SC-076-N; SC-077-C).
            Declaration-level. Each target names declared entities only. It is not a reference
            to a MODEL-DEFINITION or KIND-DEFINITION Record (076 RF-076-1, RF-076-5), not a
            domain instance, and not by itself a semantic dependency (RF-076-11; Artifact 062
            D-9). Naming a target creates, declares or admits no Model or Kind, and transfers no
            Record, authority or canonicality to the Registry (SD-4, SD-9, SD-11).
CHECK       NATIVE — presence; at least one target; no two targets identical; each target's
            parts as below.
            No check decides whether a shape §4 marks UNRESOLVED is admissible: no current
            source does, and this contract does not (§0 OUTCOMES).
BASIS       REQUIRED SYNTHESIS — 076 §7, SD-4, RF-076-1; RMS §10.2; 064 §12 Q2 (at least one
            stated scope). A target as a model with an optional Kind follows 073's domain_model
            and domain_kind and 069's subject_model and subject_kind (REPOSITORY CONVENTION).
            Carrying scope as a list of targets rather than one fixed Model/Kind pair, the
            duplicate rule and the element NAME are 077 CHOICES (§6 REPRESENTATION). None decides
            SC-076-N.
REJECT      no target — a schema that applies to nothing          (SD-4)            NATIVE
            two identical targets                                 (077 CHOICE)      NATIVE

ELEMENT     applicability.model
LAYER       FAMILY — part of each applicability target
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  one value from the closed set   W | E | P | R | V | I
              W  World       E  Epistemic   P  Production
              R  Registry    V  Visual      I  Issue
            In a Kind-scoped target, it is the Kind's owning model: it says whose Kind taxonomy
            declares applicability.kind, and widens the scope to nothing beyond that Kind. In a
            target without kind, the model is itself the stated scope — an UNRESOLVED shape (§4
            A-08). It names the declared Record Model itself — the six constitutionally
            established models are the declared models Artifact 063 admits (§7 row 2). It is a
            declaration reference, not a MODEL-DEFINITION reference (076 RF-076-5).
            R is in the set because the Registry is one of the six sovereign Record Models. That
            this contract can represent an R-scoped target does not mean any is scheduled, and
            no Registry structural contract — this one included — becomes a SCHEMA-DEFINITION
            Record by it (076 §18 row 19).
CHECK       NATIVE — presence; a single value; membership of the closed set. Membership is the
            declared-status check for a model: the closed set is the set of declared Record
            Models (Artifact 063 §7 row 2; RMS §2), so no external proof is needed.
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — any named Model is a declared Record Model, and any named Kind is a
            declared Kind "of its owning model" (076 RF-076-1; Artifact 063 §7 rows 2–3; RMS
            §2). The closed set follows 069's subject_model and 073's domain_model (REPOSITORY
            CONVENTION). Writing the model as an explicit part of every target, Kind-scoped ones
            included, is a 077 CHOICE: it puts the Kind's owning model in the Record, so the
            EXTERNAL declared-status check of applicability.kind knows whose Kind taxonomy to
            consult. The sources require that the owning model be established, not that it be a
            separate part; this choice does not make other representations unconstitutional,
            and it decides nothing about whether a schema must name a Kind, or a Model scope
            apart from its Kind (SC-077-C).
REJECT      absent — including a target that names a Kind and no model. A required carrier of
            this contract is missing; that is not a finding that the Kind is undeclared
                                                          (077 CHOICE)      NATIVE
            two or more values in one target — several scopes are several targets
                                                          (077 CHOICE)      NATIVE
            a value outside the set, e.g. S "Simulation" claimed as a seventh model
                                                          (RMS §2)          NATIVE
            a Record identifier or a MODEL-DEFINITION Record identifier, R-<kind>-…
                                                          (RF-076-5, RF-076-7)
                                                                            NATIVE

ELEMENT     applicability.kind
LAYER       FAMILY — part of each applicability target
REQUIRED    no — present in a Kind-scoped target; absent in a target that states Model scope
            only, which is UNRESOLVED (§4 A-08)
CARDINALITY zero-or-one
CONSTRAINT  names one Kind exactly as the Kind taxonomy of applicability.model declares it — for
            example CHARACTER under W. The name is read only within applicability.model. The
            value names the Kind itself — never a Record of that Kind (RF-076-7), never the
            Kind's KIND-DEFINITION Record (RF-076-5), never a two-character kind code
            (SC-077-I), never a subtype and never a runtime object (RF-076-9).
            Declared status. The named Kind must be a declared Kind of applicability.model, with
            that status established by the owning model's own Kind architecture (076 RF-076-1;
            Artifact 063 §7 row 3, §8.3). A SCHEMA-DEFINITION neither declares nor admits it,
            and creates no Kind (076 SD-4, SD-11).
            Form. applicability.kind is a declaration reference to the declared Kind, not an
            R → R reference to its KIND-DEFINITION Record (RF-076-1, RF-076-5). Naming it is not
            by itself a semantic dependency on the Kind's semantics (RF-076-11; Artifact 062
            D-9).
CHECK       NATIVE — at most one value; the value is not shaped as a Record identifier under the
            universal grammar (RMS §5); the pair (applicability.model, applicability.kind) is not
            (W, WSV).
            EXTERNAL — declared status, and that the Kind is applicability.model's. The proof
            comes from the owning model's Kind architecture (Artifact 063 SC-063-H; SC-077-K).
            This contract does not define or prove that evidence. Downstream legality validation
            may enforce this requirement under its own contract; row 112 independently enforces
            its narrower domain-instance reference prohibition. An undetermined Kind is not
            legal (Artifact 063 RB-6).
BASIS       REQUIRED SYNTHESIS — 076 RF-076-1, RF-076-5, RF-076-7, SD-4; Artifact 063 §6, §8.3,
            SC-063-G (the form of a declaration reference is fixed by the applicable family
            contract or schema). The declaration form and naming the Kind by its declared name
            follow 069's subject_kind and 073's domain_kind (REPOSITORY CONVENTION). Making the
            part optional, so that a Model-scoped target can be written and marked UNRESOLVED
            rather than made unwritable, is a 077 CHOICE (§6 REPRESENTATION; SC-077-C). The
            element NAME is a 077 CHOICE.
REJECT      two or more Kinds in one target — several scopes are several targets
                                                          (077 CHOICE)      NATIVE
            a Record identifier, e.g. W-CH-…-<slug> (a domain instance)
                                                          (RF-076-7)        NATIVE
            a KIND-DEFINITION Record's identifier, R-<kind>-…     (RF-076-5)        NATIVE
            WSV under W — "the WSV singleton is not a Kind" (Roadmap PART III)      NATIVE
            a name applicability.model has not declared — a candidate, a rejected candidate, or
            a subtype such as GENERATED-IMAGE under V              (RF-076-1)        EXTERNAL
            a declared name under the wrong model, e.g. CHARACTER under P
                                                                  (RF-076-1)        EXTERNAL
            a kind code, e.g. CH, written in place of the Kind's name
                                                                  (SC-077-I)        EXTERNAL

ELEMENT     occurrence
LAYER       FAMILY
REQUIRED    no — a Record may list no occurrence, a shape that is UNRESOLVED (§4 O-01)
CARDINALITY zero-or-more — each value is one field occurrence, with the parts occurrence.field,
            occurrence.required and occurrence.cardinality
CONSTRAINT  each value states that one field occurs in the structure the schema defines, whether
            it is required there, and how many values it may carry there. That is the schema
            side of the split: row 078's Done — "a schema composes field definitions and owns
            cardinality/required/order; a field definition owns meaning and domain" — and 076
            §8, SD-5.
            Structure, not meaning. An occurrence carries no field meaning and no field domain;
            the field's FIELD-DEFINITION stays the sole holder of both (076 §8, SD-3). Composing
            a field respects its governed meaning and domain: "A schema that carries the field
            conforms to the field's definition" (Artifact 072 §10; 076 RF-076-2).
            Not a reference. An occurrence is a structural element of the schema, not a Record
            reference, and no reference carrier is attached to it (076 RF-076-2; §6 COMPOSITION).
            No minimum. Blueprint §9.4 — "Schema defines the structure of a record — fields,
            types, required-ness, defaults." — and 064 §12 Q8 — "a schema composes fields and
            owns cardinality, requiredness and order; it is not one field" — place field
            composition on the schema side. Neither states that every SCHEMA-DEFINITION lists
            at least one field occurrence, and RMS §10.2's "required fields" is a permission
            (076 §7, SD-14). A Record with no occurrence is therefore representable and
            UNRESOLVED (§4 O-01; SC-077-O): this contract neither accepts nor rejects it. A
            Record that defines no structure at all is a different case: it does not answer its
            Kind's semantic question (076 §7), and once that is shown it is REJECT (§4 O-10).
            Each field at most once. One schema definition states one requiredness and one
            cardinality for a field, so no two occurrences name the same field.
            Order. The sequence in which occurrences are written carries no meaning defined
            here. Whether field order is significant, and how it is carried, is closed by row 078
            — "078 closes it, 077 encodes it" (076 §7) — and this contract neither establishes
            nor excludes it (SC-077-D).
CHECK       NATIVE — no two occurrences with the same occurrence.field; each occurrence's parts
            as below; zero occurrences is the UNRESOLVED shape of §4 O-01.
            EXTERNAL — that each composed field is one the applicable model's field architecture
            establishes, and that composing it respects its governed meaning and domain. Judged
            against 072 and the governing FIELD-DEFINITION Records; this contract does not
            prove it.
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — the schema side owns which fields occur, their requiredness and their
            cardinality: RMS §10.2 ("required fields · cardinality"); Blueprint §9.4; 064 §12
            Q8, Q13; row 078 Done; 076 §7, §8, SD-3, SD-5, RF-076-2. 076 §7 hands the
            representation of requiredness and cardinality to 077 ("its representation (077)").
            077 CHOICES — the entry form and its three parts, the at-most-once rule, the element
            NAME, and REQUIRED no with no minimum count (§6 REPRESENTATION).
REJECT      two occurrences naming the same field                 (077 CHOICE)      NATIVE
            any part beyond field, required and cardinality — e.g. a meaning, domain, type or
            default stated on the occurrence                      (SD-3; P-01A, P-01C)
                                                                                    NATIVE

ELEMENT     occurrence.field
LAYER       FAMILY — part of each occurrence
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  names the one field that occurs, written as the governing sources or the applicable
            model's field architecture name it — e.g. <field> in a schema applicable to
            (W, CHARACTER). The name is read within the schema's applicability. It names the
            field itself — never a Record or Record identifier (RF-076-7), never a Registry
            Record identifier, never a Kind or kind code, never a value, value set or
            vocabulary, never a constraint, a validation rule or a validator (SD-6), never a
            runtime object (RF-076-9).
            Which definition governs it. How a field's domain relates to a schema's applicability
            — and so which FIELD-DEFINITION governs a named field within this schema's scope — is
            not decided here (076 §8, SC-076-D; row 078; SC-077-D).
            Envelope fields. Whether a schema lists the seven envelope fields is not established
            (SC-077-M). Where an occurrence names one, it does not change that field's universal
            presence or role: "An envelope field binds every Record in every model." (Artifact
            033), so occurrence.required is yes.
            Name form. This contract fixes no case rule, punctuation, spelling, URI or handle
            for the name (SC-077-D).
CHECK       NATIVE — presence; a single value; the value is not shaped as a Record identifier
            under the universal grammar (RMS §5); where it is one of the seven envelope fields,
            occurrence.required is yes.
            EXTERNAL — that the value names a field the applicable model's field architecture,
            or for an envelope field RMS §4, establishes, and that it is no Kind name, kind
            code, value or runtime object.
BASIS       REQUIRED SYNTHESIS — 076 RF-076-2, SD-3, SD-5, §8; Artifact 072 §10; Artifact 063
            §7 (no declared-field category); RMS §4; Artifact 033. Carrying the field by name,
            and not by a concrete reference, is a 077 CHOICE (§6 REPRESENTATION) following 073's
            subject_field (REPOSITORY CONVENTION). The part's presence in every occurrence, and
            the element NAME, are 077 CHOICES of the entry form.
REJECT      no value                                              (077 CHOICE)      NATIVE
            two or more fields in one occurrence                  (077 CHOICE)      NATIVE
            a Record identifier, e.g. W-CH-…-<slug> (a domain instance)
                                                                  (RF-076-7)        NATIVE
            a Registry Record identifier, R-<kind>-…, in the name's place — this part carries a
            name; no reference element is defined (§6 COMPOSITION)                 NATIVE
            an envelope field, e.g. slug, with occurrence.required no
                                                                  (RMS §4; 033)     NATIVE
            a field the applicable model's field architecture does not establish
                                                                  (RF-076-2)        EXTERNAL
            a running service, validator or engine named as the field
                                                                  (RF-076-9)        EXTERNAL

ELEMENT     occurrence.required
LAYER       FAMILY — part of each occurrence
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  one value from the closed set   yes | no
              yes  the field must occur in a Record that conforms to the schema
              no   the field may be absent from such a Record
            Stated, never defaulted: an occurrence without it does not conform, and no default
            requiredness is assumed. The tokens are local to this contract. Requiredness here is
            the schema's statement about Records it applies to; it is not the requiredness of
            this contract's own carriers.
CHECK       NATIVE — presence, a single value, membership of the closed set
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — requiredness is schema-side: RMS §10.2 ("required fields"); Blueprint
            §9.4 ("required-ness"); row 078 Done; 076 §7 (representation 077's). 077 CHOICES —
            stating requiredness on every occurrence, the closed set, the token spelling and the
            no-default rule; the no-default rule follows 073 (REPOSITORY CONVENTION).
REJECT      no value                                              (077 CHOICE)      NATIVE
            a value outside the set, e.g. sometimes or a condition  (077 CHOICE)    NATIVE
            two values                                            (077 CHOICE)      NATIVE

ELEMENT     occurrence.cardinality
LAYER       FAMILY — part of each occurrence
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  how many values the field may carry where it occurs, written L..U:
              L  a whole number, 0 or more — the fewest values
              U  a whole number not less than L and not less than 1 — the most values — or *
                 for no upper bound
            For example 1..1, 0..*, 1..*, 2..5. Cardinality and requiredness are independent:
            occurrence.required says whether the field must occur, occurrence.cardinality how
            many values it carries where it does. The values are the schema's to state; this
            contract fixes no cardinality for any field of any model. It is the cardinality of a
            field in the defined schema — not a CARDINALITY line of this contract, which counts
            this contract's own carriers (§0).
CHECK       NATIVE — presence, a single value, the L..U form and its bounds
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — cardinality is schema-side: RMS §10.2 ("cardinality"); 064 §12 Q8; row
            078 Done; 076 §7 ("how many values a field occurrence may carry in the structure";
            representation 077's). 077 CHOICES — stating cardinality on every occurrence, the
            L..U notation, its bounds and the * token (§6 REPRESENTATION).
REJECT      no value                                              (077 CHOICE)      NATIVE
            a malformed value — 2..1, 0..0, -1..3, or a word such as many
                                                                  (077 CHOICE)      NATIVE
            two values                                            (077 CHOICE)      NATIVE

ELEMENT     definition
LAYER       FAMILY
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  the governed account of the schema as one definition — "the governed definition of a
            schema" (064 §12 Q1) — stated once for the Records within its applicability. A
            Registry definition "Governs; never instantiates" (RMS §6.1). Non-empty. Its
            internal form is not prescribed by this contract. Together with any occurrences, it
            must define schema structure: a Record that defines none does not answer its Kind's
            semantic question (076 §7; §4 O-10).
            What it may state. Beyond what applicability and occurrence carry, RMS §10.2 permits
            a schema definition to define constraints, relationships and validation references.
            definition may state them as definition content, and none is required (076 SD-14).
            Whether a schema's constraints are its own content or references to
            CONSTRAINT-DEFINITION Records, what relationships denotes, and which family a
            validation reference targets are not established (076 SC-076-J; SC-077-E). This
            contract fixes no form and no target for any of them. Where the content carries a
            reference:
              — a validation reference targets an admissible category only: a VALIDATION-RULE
                is a Registry definition, an admissible R → R target; a runtime validator,
                validator process or engine never is (076 RF-076-3, RF-076-9);
              — a constraint or relationship expressed as a reference targets an admissible
                category only, e.g. a CONSTRAINT-DEFINITION or RELATIONSHIP-TYPE-DEFINITION
                Record; whether they are references at all is not established (RF-076-4);
              — any other reference — to a CONTROLLED-VOCABULARY, a MODEL-DEFINITION, another
                SCHEMA-DEFINITION or any other definition — lies in no relation this family
                establishes; an admissible category alone does not authorize it (RF-076-6;
                Artifact 063 RB-5).
            A condition stated here does not make this Record a CONSTRAINT-DEFINITION, and a
            validation reference does not make it a VALIDATION-RULE or a check (076 SD-6).
            Types and defaults are schema-side (Blueprint §9.4) and never a field definition's;
            whether a SCHEMA-DEFINITION carries them is not established (076 SC-076-K). This
            contract gives them no element and neither requires nor forbids definition to state
            them (P-01C).
            What it carries none of: a field's meaning or domain (SD-3); a field occurrence, or a
            requiredness or cardinality that overrides or contradicts an occurrence's — those
            are occurrence's alone; executable behaviour — a parser, loader, check, repair,
            migration or rewrite, or a validator's verdict, state, configuration or session (076
            §9; SD-8; Blueprint §26.3b); any Record, value or current state of any model used as
            authority (RF-076-7, RF-076-8); a claim of ownership over conforming Records, or of
            admission, declaration or canonical status (SD-9, SD-11); version, supersession or
            deprecation mechanics (076 VS-076-2); a claim to own or replace a model-owned schema
            artifact (076 §6). Whether a SCHEMA-DEFINITION describes such an artifact is not
            established (076 SC-076-I): this contract neither requires nor forbids content to
            say so, and no such statement is a reference relation this family establishes.
CHECK       NATIVE — presence, a single value, non-empty.
            EXTERNAL — the content limits are semantic and not decidable from structure; they
            are judged against 076, and this contract does not claim them proven. Whether a
            reference in the content is legal is also EXTERNAL (Artifact 063; row 112). Until
            these are established the Record is at best PENDING_EXTERNAL (§0).
BASIS       REQUIRED SYNTHESIS — 076 §6, §7, §9, SD-1, SD-6, SD-7, SD-8, SD-14, RF-076-3,
            RF-076-4, RF-076-6; RMS §6.1, §10.2; 064 §12 Q1, Q4 ("the schema's defined content;
            detail is 076's"). The single carrier, the element NAME and the non-empty rule
            follow Artifacts 067, 069, 071 and 073 (REPOSITORY CONVENTION). Carrying RMS §10.2's
            constraints, relationships and validation references as definition content, and not
            as dedicated elements with fixed targets, is a 077 CHOICE (§6 REPRESENTATION).
REJECT      no value, or an empty one                             (SD-1)            NATIVE
            content shown to define no schema structure, with no occurrence to supply one
                                                          (076 §7; O-10)    EXTERNAL
            executable code or a procedure the Registry would run to check or rewrite Records
                                                          (SD-8; RMS §10.2) EXTERNAL
            a validator's verdict or run state stored as content  (076 §9; §26.3b)  EXTERNAL
            a domain instance, domain state or runtime object as the source of meaning — e.g.
            W-CH-000001-Maximus cited as what the structure should be
                                                  (RF-076-7, RF-076-8, RF-076-9)    EXTERNAL
            a reference to a running validator presented as a validation reference
                                                                  (RF-076-3)        EXTERNAL
            a reference in a relation this family does not establish, e.g. to a
            CONTROLLED-VOCABULARY Record                          (RF-076-6)        EXTERNAL
            a requiredness or cardinality that contradicts an occurrence
                                                                  (077 CHOICE)      EXTERNAL
            a statement that the schema admits, declares or owns anything
                                                                  (SD-9, SD-11)     EXTERNAL

==================================================================================================
4. APPLICABILITY AND COMPOSITION RULES — the cross-element conditions
==================================================================================================

APPLICABILITY. The table is the rule of §3 written out. A shape is a pattern of targets.

  targets    each target              shape
  none       —                        REJECT      A-01                            NATIVE
  one        model + kind             admissible  the Kind's declared status is EXTERNAL
                                                  (A-06): PENDING_EXTERNAL until established
  one        model, no kind           UNRESOLVED  A-08 — Model-level scope
  two+       any                      UNRESOLVED  A-09 — several scopes; every target is still
                                                  checked by A-02 to A-07

A-01  no applicability target                                         → REJECT     NATIVE
A-02  a target with no applicability.model, including one that names only a Kind — a
      missing carrier of this contract, not a finding about the Kind  → REJECT     NATIVE
A-03  a target with two applicability.model or two applicability.kind values
                                                                      → REJECT     NATIVE
A-04  applicability.model outside W | E | P | R | V | I                 → REJECT     NATIVE
A-05  applicability.kind shaped as a Record identifier, or (W, WSV)    → REJECT     NATIVE
A-06  applicability.kind not a declared Kind of applicability.model, or its declared status
      cannot be established when checked (Artifact 063 RB-6)          → REJECT     EXTERNAL
A-07  two identical targets                                           → REJECT     NATIVE
A-08  exactly one target, and it has no applicability.kind            → UNRESOLVED
A-09  two or more targets                                             → UNRESOLVED
A-10  outcomes follow the order of §0: a REJECT anywhere in the Record outranks A-08, A-09 and
      O-01, and an UNRESOLVED shape outranks PENDING_EXTERNAL. No shape, admissible or not, makes
      a Record CONFORMS while an EXTERNAL check is unestablished.

BASIS       REQUIRED SYNTHESIS — 076 SD-4, RF-076-1 (A-01, A-04 to A-06); Artifact 063 §7 rows
            2–3, RB-6; Roadmap PART III (A-05). 077 CHOICE — A-02 (the explicit model carrier),
            A-03, A-07, A-10, the table form and the UNRESOLVED outcome for A-08 and A-09. SOURCE
            GAP — A-08, A-09 (076 SC-076-N; SC-077-C).

What UNRESOLVED means here. A-08 and A-09 are not accepted: nothing in this contract licenses
a schema to apply at Model level or to several scopes, and a carrier able to hold the shape is
no evidence that the shape is legal. They are not rejected either: no source forbids them, and
absence of a prohibition is not a prohibition. Each stays UNRESOLVED until a governing source
settles SC-076-N. No owner is assigned by any source, row 078 included (076 SC-076-N).

COMPOSITION.

O-01  no occurrence                                                   → UNRESOLVED
O-02  an occurrence missing field, required or cardinality             → REJECT     NATIVE
O-03  two occurrences with the same occurrence.field                   → REJECT     NATIVE
O-04  occurrence.required outside yes | no                            → REJECT     NATIVE
O-05  occurrence.cardinality not of the L..U form, or out of bounds    → REJECT     NATIVE
O-06  occurrence.field shaped as a Record identifier                   → REJECT     NATIVE
O-07  occurrence.field an envelope field with occurrence.required no   → REJECT     NATIVE
O-08  a composed field not established by the applicable model's field architecture, or
      composed contrary to its governed meaning or domain             → REJECT     EXTERNAL
O-09  definition restating a requiredness or cardinality that contradicts an occurrence
                                                                      → REJECT     EXTERNAL
O-10  no occurrence, and definition content shown to define no schema structure
                                                                      → REJECT     EXTERNAL

BASIS       SOURCE FACT — the schema side owns composition, requiredness and cardinality
            (Blueprint §9.4; 064 §12 Q8; row 078 Done; 076 SD-5). REQUIRED SYNTHESIS — O-07 (RMS
            §4; Artifact 033), O-08 (076 RF-076-2; Artifact 072 §10), O-10 (076 §7). 077 CHOICE
            — O-02 to O-06, O-09 and the L..U form. SOURCE GAP — O-01 (SC-077-O).

What O-01 means. No source states that every schema definition lists at least one field
occurrence, or that one may list none (SC-077-O). A Record with no occurrence is representable and
UNRESOLVED: not accepted, so a definition that only describes structure in its content gains no
licence from this contract; not rejected, so no minimum is invented. O-10 is separate: content
shown to define no structure at all is REJECT, because such a Record does not answer its Kind's
semantic question (076 §7).

The rules fix structure only. They derive no field, requiredness, cardinality, type, default,
order, constraint or relationship for any schema of any model, and no relation between a field's
domain and the schema's applicability (076 §8; SC-076-D).

==================================================================================================
5. STRUCTURAL PROHIBITIONS
==================================================================================================

P-01A Artifact 077 introduces no element or part beyond the ten elements and five parts of §1. A
      Record carrying any of the following does not conform (NATIVE):
      — a fixed applicability pair, which would decide SC-076-N (076 SD-4; SC-077-C):
        applicable_model, applicable_kind, model_scope_only, multi_model;
      — field meaning or domain (076 SD-3, §8): meaning, field_meaning, domain, field_domain,
        semantic_definition;
      — execution or runtime structure (076 §9, SD-8; RMS §10.2): validator, validator_config,
        engine, executor, loader, callback, hook, verdict, check_result, last_validated,
        validation_state, cache, session, process, service, worker, handler, implementation,
        implementation_path, migration, repair;
      — universal semantics or ownership (076 §14, SD-9, SD-12; RMS §4): status, tier,
        lifecycle_state, canonical, history, relationship_record, owner, owns_records,
        conforming_records, admitted, declared, layer, kind_code;
      — a binding element to a model-owned schema artifact — no such relation is established,
        and none is invented (076 SC-076-I, RF-076-6): model_schema, model_schema_ref,
        schema_file, schema_path.
P-01B Artifact 077 introduces no version, revision, latest-version, supersession, replacement,
      deprecation, retirement, effective-date, migration, compatibility, retention or history
      element or mechanism, and no lifecycle or state machine. That representation is deferred
      to rows 108–110: neither defined nor permanently prohibited here (076 VS-076-2; SC-077-N).
      Whatever those rows establish stays Registry-owned, is not an envelope field (P-05) and is
      not a universal semantic shared by W, E, P, V or I (P-06).
P-01C Artifact 077 introduces no type or default element, on occurrence or anywhere else.
      Whether a SCHEMA-DEFINITION carries types and defaults is not established (076 SC-076-K;
      SC-077-F): that is a scope boundary of this contract, not a decision that a schema
      definition may never carry them, and definition may state them (§3). Types and defaults are
      never transferred to FIELD-DEFINITION by their absence here (Blueprint §9.4; Artifact 072).
P-02  No generic reference or dependency list, and no reference element the obligations of 076
      do not require: references, refs, dependencies, related_definitions, definition_refs,
      field_definition_ref, field_definition_refs, field_ref, constraint_ref, constraint_refs,
      validation_ref, validation_rule_ref, relationship_ref, vocabulary_ref,
      model_definition_ref, kind_definition_ref, schema_ref, extends, includes, inherits. A
      structural reference encodes only an obligation 076 establishes — here, the applicability
      targets — and an admissible target category alone authorizes nothing (076 RF-076-6;
      Artifact 063 RB-5). This contract requires no field-definition, vocabulary, constraint,
      relationship or validation reference, and is not a ruling that a concrete R → R
      reference to a FIELD-DEFINITION is illegal (076 RF-076-2; §6 COMPOSITION).
P-03  No element names, carries or implies ownership of a Record the schema applies to, of its
      values, or of a model-owned schema artifact; admission or declaration of a Model or Kind;
      or the conferral or removal of canonical status. The applicable model keeps its Records,
      their identity, values, lifecycle, authority, canonicality and semantic validation; the
      Registry owns this Record and governs the definition of the schema (076 §13, SD-9). A
      legal reference transfers no ownership, mutation authority, semantic authority,
      admission, canonicality or source-of-truth class (076 RF-076-10).
P-04  Not the schema of any domain Record. No element carries the fields, requiredness,
      cardinality, type or default of any particular model's Records: occurrence entries are
      what a concrete SCHEMA-DEFINITION Record states, and this contract states none. No
      CHARACTER, ORGANIZATION or other Kind's schema is defined or implied here.
P-05  No envelope field added, removed or renamed. The family elements and parts are not
      envelope fields; applicability, a field occurrence, requiredness, cardinality, version,
      status and tier never become one (RMS §4; 076 §14).
P-06  None of RMS §4's prohibited universal semantics. For this family that means: no universal
      semantic schema for W, E, P, R, V and I together; no Universal Record Base assembled from
      occurrences; no Universal Relationship Record from a schema's relationships; no Universal
      History Record for schema versions; no universal lifecycle, state model or status from a
      field a schema composes; no universal canonicality conferred by conformance; no
      universal Kind taxonomy from applicability; no universal identity composition from a
      schema's name or applicability (076 §14, SD-12).
P-07  Not another family's contract: not FIELD-DEFINITION (076 SD-3), not CONTROLLED-VOCABULARY,
      not CONSTRAINT-DEFINITION or VALIDATION-RULE (SD-6), not RELATIONSHIP-TYPE-DEFINITION
      (SD-7), and not MODEL-, KIND- or SUBTYPE-DEFINITION. No element embeds another family's
      definitions, and nothing here pre-builds rows 078, 081–082, 088–091 or 108–116.
P-08  No element records an LS-1 pairing or a lockstep partner. LS-1 is not a reference and
      creates no commit atomicity here, and no 076 ↔ 077 pair exists (076 §15; SC-077-B).
P-09  No dependency element. applicability.model and applicability.kind are declaration
      references, which are not by themselves semantic dependencies (Artifact 062 D-9; 076
      RF-076-11). No layer is assigned to SCHEMA-DEFINITION, so no layer-based dependency rule
      is applied; concrete dependency rules are row 111's (076 SC-076-L; SC-077-L).
P-10  No element represents how a schema definition is proposed, approved, deprecated or
      admitted; governance is Artifact 065's (076 §11).

