8. SOURCE CONDITIONS
==================================================================================================

SC-077-A  Req: RR-17 is carried exactly; its text is unavailable (GAP-C) and is not invented (076
          SC-076-F). Non-blocking.
SC-077-B  LS metadata. Row 077 carries LS: LS-1 and Why: LS-1. Roadmap PART III defines LS-1 as
          every Kind spec ↔ its Registry KIND-DEFINITION, and the Registry's own pairs are 064 ↔
          075 (Roadmap §0.7). A SCHEMA-DEFINITION structural contract is neither; no source
          states how row 077's label or its Why relates to PART III (076 SC-076-H). The
          metadata is preserved exactly. No LS-1 meaning, 076 ↔ 077 pair, lockstep class,
          commit atomicity, dependency or reference is invented. Recorded, not resolved; ROADMAP
          ISSUE, non-blocking.
SC-077-C  Applicability cardinality and presence (076 SC-076-N). No source states how many
          Models and Kinds one schema definition may name, whether both categories are always
          present, or whether a schema may apply at Model level without a Kind. No source assigns
          the question, row 078 included. 077 owns only the representation: a list of targets,
          each a model with an optional Kind, with the Model-level and several-target shapes
          UNRESOLVED (§4 A-08, A-09). Treatment: representable, neither accepted nor rejected;
          no admissibility decided. Writing every Kind with an explicit applicability.model
          (A-02) is a 077 CHOICE of encoding: the sources require that a named Kind be declared
          "of its owning model" (076 RF-076-1), not that the model be a separate part, and the
          carrier decides neither that a schema must state a Model scope apart from its Kind
          nor any count; a Kind-scoped target states one scope, the Kind's. Non-blocking for
          Val — every named target is a declared entity (§3) — and for Done — the structure is
          fully specified. Settling it is for a governing source; if one does, A-08 and A-09
          change through a governed change of this contract. SOURCE GAP.
SC-077-D  Field identification, name form and order (076 SC-076-D, §7). No source fixes how a
          schema identifies the fields it composes; this contract carries the field by name, a
          077 CHOICE, and fixes no case rule or spelling. Which FIELD-DEFINITION governs a named
          field within a schema's scope, and whether field order is significant, are row 078's
          (H: 076, 072). This contract preempts neither and adds nothing to row 078's Done. If
          078's closure calls for a different encoding, this contract changes through its own
          governed change. DEFERRED TO 078, non-blocking.
SC-077-E  Constraints, relationships and validation references (076 SC-076-J). No source fixes
          their form or target family. They are definition content here; no dedicated element,
          target family or relation is fixed, and any reference carried is bounded by 076
          RF-076-3, RF-076-4 and RF-076-6. The constraint/validation binder is row 113's. No
          owner is established for the form. SOURCE GAP, non-blocking.
SC-077-F  Types and defaults (076 SC-076-K). Schema-side and never a field definition's
          (Blueprint §9.4; Artifact 072); whether a SCHEMA-DEFINITION carries them is not
          established. No element is defined, none is required, and definition may state them
          (P-01C). No owner is established. SOURCE GAP, non-blocking.
SC-077-G  Model-owned schemas and → all model schemas (076 SC-076-I). The model-owned schema rows
          (§6 DOWNSTREAM) are owned by their models, carry their own canonical gates, and list
          no 077 in their H. Whether such a schema is described by, declared through or
          independent of a SCHEMA-DEFINITION Record is not established, and no element binds
          the two. The unlock is preserved; no row is edited and no dependency is added. SOURCE
          GAP and ROADMAP ISSUE, non-blocking.
SC-077-H  Row 077 carries T: schema · Canon: canonical-about-meaning · CD: yes on a docs/** path.
          Artifact 003's general convention gives a docs/** specification Canon: n/a; whether it
          reaches a structural contract is not stated (076 SC-076-M; 073 SC-073-F). The metadata
          is preserved exactly; this file is not a Registry Record, and CD: yes licenses nothing.
          Recorded, not resolved.
SC-077-I  No two-character Registry Kind code is established, and kind codes outside World are
          not frozen (Artifact 063 §9). The envelope kind is constrained symbolically,
          applicability.kind is named rather than coded, and no code is minted. Identity binding
          is row 117's.
SC-077-J  Realization and notation. The Blueprint names JSON Schema and LinkML as realization
          choices (§12.15, §26.3b). This file follows the repository's local structural-contract
          notation (§0) — Artifact 067's, with 069's CHECK line, 071's REPOSITORY CONVENTION
          label, 073's absent, and this file's dotted parts, zero-or-one, zero-or-more,
          one-or-more and the four outcomes of §0 — and adopts no serialization, schema language
          or generated validator. No repository-wide schema language is established.
SC-077-K  Declared status has no single proof mechanism across the six models (Artifact 063
          SC-063-H). applicability.kind's declared status and ownership by applicability.model
          are therefore an EXTERNAL check whose proof is the owning model's. For
          applicability.model the closed set is itself the declared set (Artifact 063 §7 row 2).
          Recorded; non-blocking.
SC-077-L  Layer placement (076 SC-076-L; Artifact 062 §6). Not established; none is assigned,
          and no layer-based dependency rule is applied. Concrete dependency rules are row 111's.
          Non-blocking.
SC-077-M  Envelope fields as occurrences. The seven envelope fields bind every Record (RMS §4;
          Artifact 033), yet no source states whether a schema definition lists them among its
          occurrences. This contract neither requires nor forbids listing them; where one is
          listed it must be required (O-07), and nothing else about it is decided. The envelope
          stays required on every Record whether or not a schema lists its fields. Recorded, not
          resolved; non-blocking.
SC-077-N  Version representation (076 SC-076-E). Deferred to rows 108–110; not defined and not
          prohibited here (P-01B). Non-blocking.
SC-077-O  Zero field occurrences. Blueprint §9.4 and 064 §12 Q8 place field composition on the
          schema side; RMS §10.2 permits a schema definition to define "required fields"; 076 §7
          requires that a schema definition define structure and reads RMS §10.2's categories
          as permissions (SD-14). No source states that every SCHEMA-DEFINITION lists at least
          one field occurrence, or that one may list none. The contract can represent zero
          occurrences (occurrence REQUIRED no) and does not admit them: such a Record is
          UNRESOLVED (O-01), and one whose content is shown to define no structure is REJECT
          (O-10). Representability is not approval. 077 owns the representation only. No source
          assigns the admissibility question — row 078's closure is the schema/field overlap,
          not this — and none is invented. SOURCE GAP; non-blocking for Val and Done.

